-- title:
--   One moduli place for all rigid-chart points over s
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`; for an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and a valuation subring $A$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, $A_0 :=$ `A.comap (algebraMap k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` is the induced valuation subring of $k_0$ and $\kappa :=$ `ResidueField A₀` its residue field.
--
--   **Data and hypotheses on the global place and the supersingular place.** A prime $q$ with $5 \le q$; a nonzero $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$; a valuation subring $A \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q}$ with `hA : A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (the subfield of `LaurentSeries (ResidueField A)` generated over `ResidueField A` by `jqModC` and `jqNModC … M'`) over `ResidueField A`, which by `hW` consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: the rational places $w$ satisfying `IsAffineGeomPlace` for which `w.evalAt (jGeomGen …)` lies in `ssJSet q …`. The hypothesis `hle` states the inclusion of intermediate fields `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`, where the left-hand side is the base change to $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ of the all-divisors level-$M'$ function field `modularFunctionFieldFull M' = IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ (divisorExpansions M')` and the right-hand side is `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, with `levelH q M'` the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, that is the subgroup of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. A constant-reduction datum $R_0$ of type `ConstantReduction A ↥(modularFunctionFieldBar M') (modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M')`, consisting of a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target field with kernel the maximal ideal, the compatibilities `algebraMap_mem_iff` and `residue_algebraMap` with $A$, the scaling clause `exists_smul_mem`, and a place map preserving degrees and transporting order functions. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\bar{\mathbb Q}((\mathsf q))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue is, as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally $s$ is a chosen element of $W$.
--
--   **Data and hypotheses on the local base ring.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$; the hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` assert that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, that $A_0$ is a henselian local ring, and that $\kappa$ is algebraically closed; `hκ` asserts that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   **Data and hypotheses on the auxiliary prime and the rigid level field.** A prime $\ell'$ with $\ell' \ne q$, $3 \le \ell'$ and $\ell' \nmid M'$; an element $\xi \in k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity, together with `hιξ`: some ring homomorphism $k_0 \to \mathbb C$ sends $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell'))$. An intermediate field $K$ of $k_0((\mathsf q))/k_0$ which by `hK` equals `laurentBaseChange k₀ (xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ')^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ') M'))`, the $k_0$-base change of the $X_H$ function field of level $(q\ell')^2M'$ for $H$ the group of units of $\mathbb Z/(q\ell')^2M'$ congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell'$; $K$ is an $A_0$-algebra, compatibly with $k_0$. An element $j \in K$, nonzero, whose image in $k_0((\mathsf q))$ is the coefficientwise image of the $\mathsf q$-expansion `jq` of the modular $j$-function.
--
--   **Functoriality hypotheses for level structures and projective models.** `hℓ`: over every $A_0$-algebra $T$, a `LevelPData D` satisfying `IsLevelPStructure W ℓ' D` still satisfies `IsLevelPStructure (C • W) ℓ' (D.variableChange C)` for every variable change $C$. `hM`: likewise `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` implies `IsGamma0PowAt (C • W) p k (kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h)`. A family of group laws $\mathcal G$ on the projective Weierstrass models over $A_0$-algebras with unit discriminant, assumed chord-and-tangent (`h𝒢`: its point functor is realised by an addition- and Galois-compatible evaluation) and origin-normalised (`h𝒢O`: the identity section is the origin chart section at which $x/y$ and $z/y$ vanish). A level transport $\mathcal T$ of raw Drinfeld pairs for $\mathcal G$ at $q$, with `h𝒯 : 𝒯.IsSectionTransport`, i.e. the curves of the transported pairs are the expected ones and the transported $P$- and $Q$-sections compose correctly with variable-change, respectively coefficient, morphisms of the graded coordinate rings. `hVC` and `hCO` assert the existence, for each variable change $C$ and each $A_0$-algebra homomorphism $f$ of coefficients, of graded ring homomorphisms of the projective coordinate rings which carry the irrelevant ideal of the target into the image of that of the source and which satisfy `IsVariableChangeHom`, respectively `IsCoefficientHom`.
--
--   Write $\mathcal R :=$ `rigidDataPow A₀ ℓ' M' q hℓ hM 𝒢 𝒯`, the rigid Weierstrass datum attached to the product of the three level components: for each $A_0$-algebra $T$, a raw point of $\mathcal R$ over $T$ is a Weierstrass curve over $T$ with unit discriminant together with (i) a family of polynomials indexed by the prime factors $p$ of $M'$ satisfying `IsGamma0PowAt` for $p^{v_p(M')}$, (ii) a `LevelPData` satisfying `IsLevelPStructure` at $\ell'$, and (iii) a raw Drinfeld pair which is a Drinfeld $q$-basis for $\mathcal G$; points are raw points modulo variable change. Write $\mathcal C :=$ `chartAlgFin A₀ K j`, the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A_0[j]$.
--
--   **Data and hypotheses on the representing package and the Tate point.** A package $P_0$ of type `LevelModuliPackageAbs A₀ 𝓡.toLevelModuliDatum`, i.e. an $A_0$-algebra $B_0$ with a point `P₀.univ` over it such that every point over every $A_0$-algebra $T$ is the image of `P₀.univ` under a unique $A_0$-algebra homomorphism $B_0 \to T$. A point $x_0$ of the datum over $K$ whose $j$-invariant `jOf x₀`, read in $k_0((\mathsf q))$, equals `jqNModC k₀ (q*ℓ')`. An $A_0$-algebra homomorphism `clC : P₀.B₀ → 𝓒` whose composite with the inclusion $\mathcal C \subseteq K$ is the classifying map `P₀.classify x₀` of $x_0$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hμ` pins the Tate point: there exist a variable change $C$ over $k_0((\mathsf q))$ and a raw point $r$ of $\mathcal R$ over $K$ such that (i) the class of $r$ is $x_0$; (ii) with $\zeta$ the unit determined by $\xi$, writing $(P_1,P_2) :=$ `cuspPoint k₀ (q*ℓ') ζ ![1,0]`, which is the Tate toric point `tateToricPoint k₀ (q*ℓ') ζ`, one has $C.u \cdot (2P_1 + \tfrac16) = 2P_2 + P_1$ and $C.r = -\tfrac1{12}$, $C.s = -\tfrac12$, $C.t = \tfrac1{24}$ as constant Laurent series; (iii) the curve of $r$, pushed to $k_0((\mathsf q))$, is $C \bullet$ `tateBase k₀ (q*ℓ')`; (iv) for every prime factor $p$ of $M'$, every field $F'$, every ring homomorphism $f : k_0 \to F'$ and every primitive $p^{v_p(M')}$-th root of unity $\zeta' \in F'$, the $\Gamma_0$-component polynomial `r.level.1 p`, pushed to $k_0((\mathsf q))$ and then mapped coefficientwise by $f$, equals `kernelVariableChangeDeg (C.map (coeffMap f)) (gamma0PowDeg p (M'.factorization p))` applied to $\prod (X - (\mathrm{toricPoint}\, F'\,(q\ell')\,\zeta'^a)_1)$, the product over $1 \le a \le p^{v_p(M')}/2$ with $p \nmid a$; (v) the $\ell'$-level component `r.level.2.1`, pushed to $k_0((\mathsf q))$, is `(cuspData k₀ (q*ℓ') ζ ![q,0] ![0,-q]).variableChange C`; (vi) there are elements $P_x, P_y, Q_x, Q_y$ of $K$ whose images in $k_0((\mathsf q))$ are the four coordinates `xP`, `yP`, `xQ`, `yQ` of `(cuspData k₀ (q*ℓ') ζ ![ℓ',0] ![0,-ℓ']).variableChange C`, and the Drinfeld sections `r.level.2.2.P` and `r.level.2.2.Q` pass through $(P_x,P_y)$ and $(Q_x,Q_y)$ in the sense of `IsSectionThrough`.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists a single place $v$ of `modularFunctionFieldFullC κ M'` over $\kappa$ — the subfield of $\kappa((\mathsf q))$ generated over $\kappa$ by the series `qExpand κ d (jqModC κ)` for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $M'$ — such that the following holds for every maximal ideal $y$ of $\mathcal C$ and every $A_0$-algebra homomorphism $\psi : \mathcal C \to \kappa$ whose vanishing locus is exactly $y$ (that is, $\psi(c) = 0$ if and only if $c \in y$).
--
--   Assume that $y$ lies over $s$ in the following sense: for every $g \in \mathbb Q((\mathsf q))$ lying in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` such that the corresponding element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers`, such that $g$ has non-negative order at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ at which the element coming from `jq` has non-negative order, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, and for which moreover `qExpand k₀ ℓ' (coeffEmb k₀ g)` — the series obtained from $g$ by substituting $\mathsf q^{\ell'}$ — lies in $K$ and in $\mathcal C$: for every $c \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$ and whose residue in `ResidueField A` equals `s.evalAt` applied to the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference between that element of $\mathcal C$ and the image of $c$ under `algebraMap A₀ 𝓒` lies in $y$.
--
--   Then for every raw point $x$ of $\mathcal R$ over $\kappa$ whose class in the points of $\mathcal R$ over $\kappa$ equals the image of `P₀.univ` under the datum's map along $\psi \circ$ `clC`, and for every point $g$ of the affine curve `x.curve` over $\kappa$ satisfying the two conditions that $g$ has additive order $M'$ and that for every prime factor $p$ of $M'$, every $n \in \mathbb N$ and every nonsingular pair $(x_1,y_1)$ with $n \cdot g = (x_1,y_1)$ and $n \cdot g$ of additive order $p^{v_p(M')}$ the element $x_1$ is a root of the polynomial `x.level.1 p`, the class of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-pair (`x.curve`, $g$) in `ModuliPoint M' κ` has $v$ as a moduli place: `IsModuliPlaceOf κ M'` holds of that moduli point and $v$, that is, there are a field $\Omega$ with a $\kappa$-algebra structure and a `ModuliTestDatum κ M'` for that moduli point over $\Omega$ — a place of $\Omega$ over $\kappa$, a Weierstrass curve over its valuation ring with nonzero reduced discriminant, a point of additive order $M'$, a retraction of the residue field onto $\kappa$ fixing $\kappa$, the identification of the reduced pair with the given moduli point, and an embedding `emb` of `modularFunctionFieldFullC κ M'` into $\Omega$ satisfying the `emb_jqNFull` compatibility with cyclic-quotient $j$-invariants — for which the valuation subring of $v$ is the preimage under `emb` of the valuation subring of that place.
--
--   The force of the statement is that $v$ is chosen before $y$, $\psi$, $x$ and $g$, hence is common to all closed points of the chart $\mathcal C$ lying over the single place $s$ and to all admissible level-$M'$ generators on the corresponding curves.
--
--   This is the uniformity step in the study of the characteristic-$q$ specialisation of the rigid full-level moduli chart: all closed points of the integral chart $\mathcal C$ over one supersingular place $s$, with their $\Gamma_0(M')$-level generators, give moduli points of the level-$M'$ moduli problem admitting one and the same moduli place of the all-divisors level-$M'$ function field over $\kappa$. It is cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.forall_nsmul_eq_zero_and_exists_variableChange_of_over_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataPow_of_tatePoint`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.forall_nsmul_eq_zero_and_exists_variableChange_of_over_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataPow_of_tatePoint), which combines it with the torsion and variable-change information at the same points.
